{#- The backdrop: the celestial body, three hill silhouettes cut from one
    drawing by tools/gen-hills.py, and the torii gate standing on the near
    hill.

    ORDER IS DEPTH here, and it is the whole of how the pieces relate:

      the orb    furthest back, behind everything
      hill 3, 2  the far and middle hills
      the gate   in front of both, behind the near hill
      hill 1     nearest, painting over the gate's feet

    The three hills share one viewBox, so they need no offsets of their own:
    the stylesheet places the box and every hill lands where it belongs
    inside it. The orb and the gate are not placed that way — each is a
    bounded object with a box, which is why neither carries a `hill` class
    and neither picks up their placement rule.

    THE ORB IS ALSO THE THEME SWITCH, where the including page asks for it.
    It ships DISABLED and aria-hidden and theme.js removes both, which is the
    same bargain the icon toggle makes with its `hidden`: without JavaScript
    there is nothing for a control to do, so it stays what it was, a drawing
    of a sun. A focusable button that does nothing is worse than no button.

    That is also why aria-hidden is on each decorative child rather than on
    the box around them — a focusable element inside an aria-hidden subtree is
    hidden from a screen reader while still taking a tab stop, which is the
    one arrangement worse than either.

    Dropping any of these is a matter of deleting its line, which is how this
    is meant to be reused at the foot of an inner page. Leave `orbToggles`
    unset there and the orb is decoration again. #}
<div class="hills">
  {%- if orbToggles %}
  <button class="orb" type="button" data-theme-toggle disabled aria-hidden="true"></button>
  {%- else %}
  <span class="orb" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  {%- endif %}
  <span class="hill hill-3" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="hill hill-2" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="torii" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="hill hill-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</div>
